# CliffCS₂ derives the decoded relations of its sources

On one wire and none: the decoding of every relation of Bian and Selinger's
presentation of `Uₘ(ℤ[½, i])` in dimensions `2` and `1`, refined by the
new scalar `w` (`w` central, `w² = i`), is derivable from Figure 6
(`W1.rel_derivable`, `W0.rel_derivable`), and decoding the encoding of a
generator derives it (`W1.DE_gen`, `W0.DE_gen`).  The paper does not treat
these widths.  Each derivation was found by a search over rewrites modulo
commuting gates on disjoint wires, using the one-wire rules of Figure 6,
and is replayed by `derive`.

Generated by `gen/gen_cs.py` from the derivations `gen/run_cs.py` finds.
-/
import QCert.Minimality.CliffordCS.Transfer
import QCert.Minimality.Derive

namespace QCert.Minimality.CliffordCS

open QCert.Circuit

/-- The theory of Figure 6. -/
abbrev Th : CRel Gate := Padded (pres.Base fun _ => True)

theorem hsc : ∀ c c' : Gate 0, c = c' := by intro c c'; cases c; cases c'; rfl

/-- Letters of words written out: a gate and the wire it starts on. -/
inductive Lt
  | w | H | S | CS | SW

/-- The generator of `n`-wire circuits for a letter (the scalar for a
letter that does not fit). -/
def Lt.gen : (n : ℕ) → Lt → ℕ → Gen Gate n
  | _, .w, 0 => .gate0 .ω
  | _ + 1, .H, 0 => .gate1 .H
  | _ + 1, .S, 0 => .gate1 .S
  | _ + 2, .CS, 0 => .gate2 .CS
  | _ + 2, .SW, 0 => .gate2 .swap
  | n + 1, g, o + 1 => .up (Lt.gen n g o)
  | _, _, _ => .gate0 .ω

/-- A word written in time order (the first letter applied first). -/
def tw (n : ℕ) (l : List (Lt × ℕ)) : Circuit Gate n :=
  FreeMonoid.ofList (l.reverse.map fun x => x.1.gen n x.2)


/-- The decoding of every relation of Bian and Selinger's presentation in
dimension `2` is derivable on one wire. -/
